# Gate step — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq). Wired by 1087-h2z9.
#
# Triaged from scripts/gate-divergence-declared.txt, where it sat `untriaged`
# since 2026-09-06: present in --ci-full, absent from --check, nobody decided.
# Measured green and cheap on b026372ff (Version monotonicity), so the honest verdict is to run
# it where every host lands rather than once a day on the release gate.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf): a binding assembled
# from a variable is invisible to every name-based scan.
STEP_DESC="Checking VERSION is monotonic against the last release"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/verify-version-monotonic.sh"
STEP_ERROR="VERSION is not monotonically >= the last release (1087-h2z9)"
STEP_OK="Version monotonicity passed"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="macneo 2026-09-22 darwin ok:rc0-no-verdict-line"
# ORDER 2157-ginp: the paths this step reads, RECORDED ONLY (not yet used to
# skip it; that waits on an operator ruling). First cut: the step's own script
# plus every repo path it names literally.
STEP_INPUTS="scripts/hooks/pre-push-local-gate.sh scripts/verify-version-monotonic.sh"
